    "A morning in the studio",
    "Notes from a photography review",
    "Project update",
    "Morning light filled the studio as the team\nreviewed a new collection of photographs.\nEach image told a small part of the story.",
    "The first review focused on composition.\nWe compared the balance of light and\nshadow, then wrote a few practical notes.",
    "Later, we returned to the strongest ideas.\nSmall changes made the images easier to\nread without changing their character.",
    "Review checklist",
    "1. Keep related lines in one paragraph.\nWrapped text should stay with its item.",
    "2. Leave a clear gap before the next idea.\nPreserve the original reading order.",
    "3. Keep the two columns separate.\nSelecting a passage should highlight\nonly the words that belong to it.",
    "The review ended with a short list of\nchanges to try during the next session.",
